this is a major development in this case  as you say what has happened here over  the years that this hospital trust has  already been described as the worst  maternity scandal in the history of the  NHS and now the police are getting  involved they are seeing if it amounts  to what if what has happened here  amounts to criminal behavior we've had a  statement in the last few minutes from  the assistant Chief Constable of West  Mercia Police he says today we've met  with NHS improvement the Department of  Health and the independent reviewer to  discuss complaints made against  Shrewsbury and Telford NHS Hospital  Trust in relation to maternity services  and provision the independent review is  ongoing he says we can confirm that a  police investigation will be conducted  to explore whether there is evidence to  support a criminal case either against  the trust or any individuals involved  the investigation is now live he says so  we are unable to comment any further at  this time and he urges any family that  has not been in touch with the ongoing  independent review to get in touch with  police now we know that over a thousand  cases are being looked into we know that  this trust has already paid out millions  of pounds in damages to families who  suffered the avoidable loss of their  babies due to mistakes made in maternity  care we know that dozens of babies have  died unavoidably over the years here  some mothers - and we also know that  there are many babies who've been left  brain damage now what began as an  investigation led by an independent  midwife in 2017 into 23 possible cases  of clinical malpractice has now spiraled  to the point where as you say hundreds  over 1,600 families now in touch with  that independent inquiry now these are  families that have suffered here over  since 1979 but many of those I'm told  are much closer to the present day and  indeed I understand that the most recent  case being investigated is the death of  a baby this year the families  who have lost babies have long said that  this is a trust that has failed to learn  lessons and that is why mistakes are  repeated they have always said that the  needs to be accountability as I say  there is this ongoing independent review  into these cases that's not due to  report possibly until early next year  due to the huge number of families that  have come forward the huge number of  cases to look into but this police  investigation will now run in tandem  with that looking to see whether what  happened either as a result of the trust  or indeed individuals that have worked  here over the years whether there has  been criminal behavior as the police say  it is now a live investigation so they  won't be commenting any further we have  this evening contacted the trust for  their reaction to this major development  and we are awaiting their response to  this ok Becky thank you very much indeed
 

